    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") flag for owner creation.\n\n**Behavior:** When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive) and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (earliest match when several). Otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false` and `possibleDuplicateOf` is absent.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added two `@Transient` fields `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` with getters/setters, mirroring the existing per-request `bulkSignupWarning` pattern (not persisted).\n\n2. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function) \u2014 scans `ownerRepository.findAll()`, excluding itself by id, for an owner with the same last name and postcode but a different telephone; sets the flag and the matched id. A matching telephone is skipped since that would be a hard duplicate (rejected earlier by `CheckIdentityUnique`).\n\n3. **Pipelines** \u2014 wired the new step into both `owners.POST.yml` (after save, like `FlagBulkSignup`) and `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`. Because these flags are transient and recomputed on read, the GET path must recompute them too \u2014 which is exactly how the acceptance test reads them back.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` response schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them.\n\nThe target test `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
